Faithful reconstruction of FUN_0000_fd79 (SOUND.CFG parser): thread the open CF, restore the [0x70]
string-segment base on the keyword-table reads, and fix 16-bit word pointer scaling.

fd79 opens SOUND.CFG (via fefb) and, on success, parses it against a keyword table held in the engine's
far string segment (DGROUP:0x70 -> image para 0x2d74). Four Ghidra losses converged to a SIGSEGV (incl. the dropped SI template offset):
 (a) FLAGS: the `jb fdd8` testing the open's CF became a dead `in_CF=0` local -> the parse block ran even
     when the open failed. Threaded from the INT reg-file CF slot uRam000f0012.
 (b) SEGMENT: `lods es:[si]` with ES = the [0x70] string segment lost its base -> `*(int*)0x212` host
     deref. Rebased to STRSEG (linear 0x2d740) + SI; the `mov [bx],ah` store rebased to DGROUP:bx.
 (c) SCALING: the word table was typed `int*` (4 bytes in the flat model) -> wrong reads and stride.
     Read uint16_t, advance by 2.
Loop logic and the DGROUP SB-config writes (0x4f4/0x4f6/0x4f8) and error-path service icalls are
preserved verbatim. Classes: CF-flag threading + SS/[0x70] dynamic-segment scratch + pointer scaling.

